{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The binary-size budget, the "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lifecycle guarantee, and the re-render characteristics of the default placeholders — what’s measured, what’s guaranteed, and why.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Performance"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Performance","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"ScreenStates’ pitch is “small, dependency-free, drop into any screen.” This article covers the three ways that’s kept measurable rather than just assumed: a CI-enforced size budget, an audited concurrency guarantee, and a documented rendering characteristic."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"The-binary-size-budget","text":"The binary-size budget"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"CI builds ","type":"text"},{"code":"swift build -c release","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on every push and sums the resulting ","type":"text"},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" sizes for the ","type":"text"},{"code":"ScreenStates","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" target, failing the build if that total exceeds the budget committed in ","type":"text"},{"code":".github\/binary-size-budget.json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". There’s no single linked artifact to measure instead — the library product is “automatic,” and nothing in the package’s own build graph links it standalone — so the ","type":"text"},{"code":".o","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" total is the closest deterministic proxy available.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A legitimate feature addition that grows this total past the budget isn’t blocked forever: bump "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxBytes"},{"type":"text","text":" in that file as part of the same PR, the same way a dependency lockfile gets updated alongside the change that needed it. The job never bumps it on its own."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"The Task lifecycle guarantee","anchor":"The-Task-lifecycle-guarantee","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"refreshCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"loadWithRetry","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" each store their running "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" in a private "},{"code":"currentTask","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" property, read by "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"deinit","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every one of those "},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s captures "},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" as "},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", not strongly — audited specifically to rule out a "},{"code":"self -> currentTask -> closure -> self","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" retain cycle keeping a store alive after its last external reference is dropped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In practice, a completed ","type":"text"},{"code":"Task","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" releases its closure’s captures on return regardless of capture style, so this mostly matters for a still-","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"running"}]},{"type":"text","text":" operation: without "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[weak self]"},{"type":"text","text":", a store couldn’t become eligible for deallocation until that operation finished, even once every other reference to it was already gone. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ConcurrencyAndCancellation"},{"type":"text","text":" for the rest of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"type":"text","text":" lifecycle — cancellation, overlapping calls, and the automatic cancel-on-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deinit"},{"type":"text","text":" safety net this guarantee supports."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Re-render characteristics of the default placeholders","anchor":"Re-render-characteristics-of-the-default-placeholders","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" only ever go active once "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refresh(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/refreshCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" have confirmed "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" is already "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — both fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"text":" otherwise, which never touch either property. That means ","type":"text"},{"code":"isRefreshing","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refreshError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can never be observed alongside ","type":"text"},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":".error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so none of the three default placeholders can ever be on screen mid-refresh.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A parent view that reads "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.state"},{"type":"text","text":" (via "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":") and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" — the pattern "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" uses for a refresh toast — still has its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":" re-evaluated whenever either changes, same as any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" property read in a SwiftUI "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"body"},{"type":"text","text":". This guarantee is about "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"which","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" placeholder that re-evaluation could ever affect, not about avoiding the re-evaluation itself: since a default placeholder is only ever on screen while "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" are both inactive, that re-evaluation never has a placeholder to needlessly re-render in the first place — only whatever renders the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case could be affected."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/performance"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateStore/refresh(_:)":{"abstract":[{"text":"Like ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/load(_:)"},{"text":", but keeps any data already in ","type":"text"},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on screen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while ","type":"text"},{"code":"operation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" runs instead of switching to ","type":"text"},{"code":".loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"pattern behind pull-to-refresh, where the list shouldn’t disappear","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while it’s being refetched. ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"duration. On success ","type":"text"},{"code":"s